The fringe spacing is $\Delta y = \dfrac{\lambda L}{d}$ (from $d\sin\theta = m\lambda$ for small angles). Any two of:

- move the screen further from the slits (increase $L$);
- decrease the separation of the slits (decrease $d$);
- use light of a longer wavelength (lower frequency), e.g. a red laser instead of a green one.

Any two of:

- no nuclear fusion occurs in its core (it shines only from stored heat);
- low luminosity;
- high surface temperature (white/blue-white colour);
- very small size (about the size of the Earth) and therefore extremely high density.

(These place white dwarfs at the bottom left of the H–R diagram.)
